{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact clean pushed head fbf032aa2ac236425af7bba0a6d63e4137f18ddf on request/operator-chain-authority, against request 00d0f2ac and artifacts d7fc0d02 (SKILL.md) and dce945d9 (AGENTS.md). Verified on a clean detached checkout: one commit resting on 00d0f2ac, diff is exactly the two files, git diff --check clean, make docs green (internal/docset 39s). I read the whole diff. The substance is right and carefully bounded: the narrow path is gated on four facts that must all be in the durable record — the requester held the adoption authority when they signed the governing request, the conditions explicitly commissioned the decision and authorized the follow-on work rather than advice or a draft, the decision artifact was delivered through that chain, independently approved and merged so the request is satisfied, and chain and artifact are effective and unretired when the follow-on begins; every missing fact, a different required ratifier, an ordinary-participant requester, an advice-only request or a stale or retired basis sends the actor back to propose-and-ratify; a changed decision is a new decision and a successor artifact inherits no adoption by path; provenance is complete for both assigned work (request rests on R and D, commit on the request) and requester-as-performer (commit on R and D, artifact on the same bases, review request on R, D and the artifact) with a worked example; staleness before start requires a refile or fresh adoption. I confirmed no software enforces the old ceremony — the only propose-specific code is the kind definition with its role:ratifier satisfier in internal/workroom/kinds.go, and neither reviewguard nor the merge preflight requires a ratified proposal — so a documentation-only head is the correct shape for the request's conditional, and the text implies no enforcement it does not have. Two bounded edits before approval. ONE (Security, authority escalation and provenance forgery): because nothing in software checks the four facts, they are checked by nobody the text names. A commit trailer resting on R and D asserts the chain; the fold will admit it whether or not R's requester held ratifier at signing or R's conditions authorized implementation. Assign the check explicitly: state in the Notes and decisions section that the independent reviewer of any work resting on an authority-bearing request chain confirms each of the four facts from the record before approving, and add the same clause to the Security bullet of AGENTS.md step 4 and SKILL.md's review guidance, so the human gate that replaces the ratification act is named rather than assumed. TWO (precision): the gate says the chain must be effective, current and unretired, but current is not a projected fact; the fold's vocabulary is effective, retired and stale. Replace current with not stale (or define it as such) so a reviewer can verify it from the projection, and say that ordinary staleness arising after the follow-on begins is recorded at merge under the existing rules rather than reopening adoption — the text already handles the before-start case and should close the after-start one in a sentence. ARCHITECTURE: repository policy (AGENTS.md) and application guidance (SKILL.md) only; no kernel, fold, projection or surface contract changes; consistent with the architecture page's placement of both files. SECURITY, beyond point one: role timing is correctly pinned to signing time so later grants cannot elevate an old request; the bases are signed durable records so the chain itself cannot be forged without keys; the satisfied-by-merge requirement means the decision passed independent review before it can authorize anything; stale or retired bases are excluded. SIMPLIFICATION: the restructuring into two named paths reads cleanly and removes the double ratification the operator objected to; nothing to cut. Fix the two points in a successor head and I will re-review promptly.","body":{"artifact":"g